WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.001 --> 00:00.944
(All characters, locations, and events are fictional

3
00:00.969 --> 00:01.920
and for entertainment purposes only.

4
00:01.944 --> 00:02.887
No actions depicted are intended to be encouraged or endorsed.

5
00:02.912 --> 00:03.960
Animals were specially trained and supervised by professionals.

6
00:03.985 --> 00:05.404
Viewer discretion is advised.)

7
00:05.846 --> 00:07.972
In golf, you can calculate everything.

8
00:07.997 --> 00:10.195
Distance, wind speed, and slope.

9
00:12.215 --> 00:14.216
But you can't calculate feelings.

10
00:16.522 --> 00:19.238
If you ask me what the most stressful moment in golf is,

11
00:19.263 --> 00:22.011
for me, it's not when I'm standing over the final putt.

12
00:22.036 --> 00:23.600
It's when I have to choose.

13
00:28.874 --> 00:31.471
Do I play it safe or take the risk?

14
00:35.071 --> 00:38.663
Sometimes the best shot isn't the safest one.

15
00:40.094 --> 00:41.310
Love is the same.

16
00:41.335 --> 00:44.216
Sometimes you have to take a risk to reach the green.

17
00:47.837 --> 00:49.273
Because if you never take the shot,

18
00:49.298 --> 00:51.868
you'll never know how close you could've gotten.

19
00:53.909 --> 00:56.202
(Pro Pop: Ploychompoo Wilairungrueng)

20
01:06.008 --> 01:09.533
♪ Everyone can tell by the way you stare ♪

21
01:10.171 --> 01:11.902
♪ Sneaking little looks when I'm unaware ♪

22
01:11.927 --> 01:15.333
♪ It's plain to see ♪

23
01:15.986 --> 01:17.837
♪ I know exactly what you think of me ♪

24
01:17.862 --> 01:21.197
♪ First to watch my stories every time ♪

25
01:21.706 --> 01:23.516
♪ You remember every fave of mine ♪

26
01:23.541 --> 01:27.099
♪ Everywhere I go, you're by my side ♪

27
01:27.467 --> 01:29.397
♪ Don't tell me there's nothing on your mind ♪

28
01:29.422 --> 01:32.201
♪ So when are you gonna say the words? ♪

29
01:32.226 --> 01:34.226
♪ Don't keep me waiting till it hurts ♪

30
01:34.251 --> 01:37.015
♪ The way you act, I know you're into me ♪

31
01:37.040 --> 01:39.731
♪ That racing heart gives you away so easily ♪

32
01:39.756 --> 01:43.727
♪ But I'll play clueless, just wait and see ♪

33
01:43.752 --> 01:45.752
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

34
01:45.777 --> 01:48.456
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

35
01:48.481 --> 01:52.022
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

36
01:52.047 --> 01:56.836
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

37
01:56.861 --> 01:58.861
♪ Or should I be the one to call your bluff? ♪

38
02:00.399 --> 02:02.069
We're going to a fashion show?

39
02:03.215 --> 02:04.905
Hello, Fahsai!

40
02:04.930 --> 02:07.708
This is my team. And this is Pro Vee.

41
02:07.870 --> 02:10.299
Fahsai! You didn't tell me you were coming.

42
02:10.324 --> 02:12.967
We can talk about that fashion show idea of yours.

43
02:12.992 --> 02:15.249
I don't really exercise at all.

44
02:15.274 --> 02:18.721
Give golf a try. I promise you'll fall for it.

45
02:18.746 --> 02:20.295
You could start with just nine holes.

46
02:20.382 --> 02:22.805
- Feeling possessive? - Jealous.

47
02:25.113 --> 02:27.872
Am I allowed to be jealous over you?

48
02:27.975 --> 02:29.626
Good question.

49
02:29.674 --> 02:32.528
If you do, you'd better start staking your claim.

50
02:32.697 --> 02:34.713
Hello, my Nana.

51
02:35.891 --> 02:38.266
A clothing collection for golfers.

52
02:38.291 --> 02:40.243
The collars need to be crisp. Yes.

53
02:40.268 --> 02:42.300
And the fabric has to breathe.

54
02:42.325 --> 02:43.546
In hot weather,

55
02:43.570 --> 02:46.014
uncomfortable clothes will only put people in a bad mood.

56
02:47.419 --> 02:49.347
Soft, but not soft enough.

57
02:49.372 --> 02:53.063
The texture needs to feel effortlessly luxurious.

58
02:54.478 --> 02:58.809
Yes. Effortlessly luxurious.

59
03:04.202 --> 03:05.527
Sorry to interrupt, Nana.

60
03:06.535 --> 03:09.003
I wanted to update you on our new memberships.

61
03:09.151 --> 03:13.206
New memberships are up 15 percent this month.

62
03:13.231 --> 03:16.020
Great. Another 15 percent softer would be perfect.

63
03:16.694 --> 03:19.537
I meant the number of members.

64
03:20.172 --> 03:21.703
Oh! Right. That's great.

65
03:21.727 --> 03:24.636
Our membership has really gone up.

66
03:24.874 --> 03:26.985
Okay. One more thing.

67
03:27.830 --> 03:31.357
I wanted to ask you about the new grass for the greens.

68
03:31.685 --> 03:33.665
We've got two options from the supplier.

69
03:33.689 --> 03:37.316
The first has good green speed but requires more maintenance.

70
03:37.341 --> 03:40.660
The other is more durable, but the speed isn't as good.

71
03:40.685 --> 03:41.938
What do you think, Nana?

72
03:41.963 --> 03:44.247
If it needs too much care, it won't work.

73
03:44.272 --> 03:47.078
We also have to consider washing, ironing, and maintenance.

74
03:48.157 --> 03:52.296
Now I'm confused. What exactly are you talking about?

75
03:53.280 --> 03:56.054
- The texture. - The texture of the grass?

76
03:57.410 --> 04:00.758
So we'll go with something durable and low-maintenance.

77
04:00.783 --> 04:04.850
It should feel soft and effortlessly luxurious.

78
04:05.310 --> 04:09.076
Wow. That's deep.

79
04:09.101 --> 04:12.413
I forgot about how the green feels underfoot.

80
04:12.438 --> 04:15.757
Okay, then. We'll go with that grass.

81
04:21.314 --> 04:24.386
This one's good too. It'll be comfortable during a swing,

82
04:24.411 --> 04:26.411
and it'll look elegant in motion.

83
04:31.450 --> 04:33.174
Are you busy, Nana?

84
04:33.356 --> 04:35.047
Vee. What's up?

85
04:35.213 --> 04:39.680
Nut said you chose a durable green with slower ball speed?

86
04:39.705 --> 04:42.772
- I haven't chosen anything yet. - Then what's going on?

87
04:42.797 --> 04:45.298
This isn't soft enough. We need the softer one.

88
04:45.323 --> 04:47.076
- The grass? - The fabric.

89
04:47.906 --> 04:51.225
Weren't we talking about the green and what grass to use?

90
04:51.250 --> 04:54.037
Oh! Right. The grass.

91
04:54.221 --> 04:56.635
Vee, what do you think of this fabric? Nice texture?

92
04:56.660 --> 04:58.107
It'd make a beautiful green.

93
04:58.132 --> 04:59.766
- Nana. - Yes?

94
04:59.790 --> 05:01.863
Which one of us is confused here?

95
05:01.888 --> 05:05.032
Sorry. Fabric and grass are all mixed up in my head.

96
05:06.509 --> 05:08.143
Maybe focus on one thing at a time.

97
05:08.168 --> 05:10.651
No one can focus on two things at once.

98
05:11.500 --> 05:13.678
Oh, Vee. Don't move.

99
05:15.888 --> 05:18.124
- Be my model. - What?

100
05:18.149 --> 05:21.526
Remember the fashion show I want to hold here?

101
05:21.551 --> 05:23.777
Besides professional models and celebrities,

102
05:23.802 --> 05:26.483
I want our pros and staff to walk the runway too.

103
05:28.594 --> 05:29.799
You think that's a good idea?

104
05:30.029 --> 05:31.394
Why wouldn't it be?

105
05:31.419 --> 05:34.595
You're gorgeous and cool, and Nut's so handsome.

106
05:34.620 --> 05:37.892
Everyone at our course is ridiculously good-looking.

107
05:40.231 --> 05:42.896
Come on. Since you're here, let me take your measurements.

108
06:04.842 --> 06:06.862
Isn't the measuring tape enough?

109
06:06.887 --> 06:10.116
You don't need to measure me with your eyes too. You're staring.

110
06:10.522 --> 06:14.720
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

111
06:15.504 --> 06:20.123
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

112
06:20.641 --> 06:25.185
♪ Together, we'll race toward the line ♪

113
06:25.751 --> 06:29.144
♪ Chasing the dream that's yours and mine ♪

114
06:29.169 --> 06:30.213
Are you done yet?

115
06:31.561 --> 06:35.270
Not yet. I still need to measure... here.

116
06:37.545 --> 06:42.277
I wonder if someone's already in your heart.

117
06:42.302 --> 06:45.465
Are all four chambers already taken?

118
06:45.490 --> 06:49.062
I wonder if there's any room for your Nana.

119
06:49.975 --> 06:55.822
What if I gave you all four? Could you take care of them?

120
06:55.858 --> 06:59.152
Of course. As long as I'm the only one in there.

121
07:01.521 --> 07:04.632
♪ And walk with me along the way ♪

122
07:04.657 --> 07:07.269
♪ No matter what it takes to win someday ♪

123
07:07.726 --> 07:10.226
Stealing a drop without permission?

124
07:10.251 --> 07:12.733
That's a penalty under the rules of golf.

125
07:13.188 --> 07:16.282
Hmm... What should the penalty be?

126
07:16.482 --> 07:18.982
Now you have to even things out.

127
07:26.758 --> 07:31.234
Clever and sneaky as ever, Miss Nana.

128
07:34.722 --> 07:39.440
♪ One look in your eyes is all I need ♪

129
07:39.465 --> 07:43.062
♪ Oh, baby. I trust your sweet. ♪

130
07:49.521 --> 07:51.076
What can I do for you, Ms. Yupadee?

131
07:52.464 --> 07:54.420
Have you seen the news about Goodview's event?

132
07:55.246 --> 07:58.393
You mean the fashion show?

133
08:00.189 --> 08:02.531
- I have. - What do you think?

134
08:03.082 --> 08:06.234
They must be running out of ideas to compete with us.

135
08:06.695 --> 08:08.996
That's why they're resorting to something so ridiculous.

136
08:09.166 --> 08:13.516
It's a golf course. It's right there in the name.

137
08:14.906 --> 08:17.023
Nana must've lost her mind.

138
08:18.081 --> 08:21.033
You really think so?

139
08:22.532 --> 08:23.810
From what I've seen,

140
08:23.834 --> 08:26.690
Goodview's event is getting a lot of attention.

141
08:27.471 --> 08:28.907
And the feedback is good.

142
08:29.451 --> 08:31.522
People are probably interested because it's unusual.

143
08:32.579 --> 08:35.972
It's a publicity stunt to get people talking.

144
08:36.496 --> 08:38.869
The buzz will die down soon enough.

145
08:39.309 --> 08:40.708
It won't last.

146
08:43.002 --> 08:44.304
And what about my course?

147
08:45.929 --> 08:49.896
You said you had new ideas, but I haven't seen a single one.

148
08:50.009 --> 08:53.360
All you've done is poach Goodview's former staff.

149
08:56.354 --> 08:57.978
Take it easy, Ms. Yupadee.

150
08:58.939 --> 09:00.788
It's not that I don't have a plan.

151
09:01.838 --> 09:04.398
I'm just waiting for the right moment.

152
09:06.568 --> 09:07.774
With something like this,

153
09:08.850 --> 09:10.706
if we're gonna play, we play hard.

154
09:12.725 --> 09:16.199
Hard enough to leave them speechless.

155
09:27.712 --> 09:30.569
Everyone's outfits have been updated and are ready.

156
09:30.594 --> 09:32.594
After practice, let's go try them on.

157
09:32.619 --> 09:37.256
Sure. But I want to walk the runway too. I've been practicing.

158
09:37.289 --> 09:39.880
They say models need a proper model face.

159
09:39.905 --> 09:43.805
Smile, raise the brows, relax the lips... and walk.

160
09:44.217 --> 09:46.256
Absolutely. I'll make you an outfit too.

161
09:46.281 --> 09:47.533
Okay!

162
09:47.683 --> 09:51.389
Actually, no. I need to handle the food and drinks.

163
09:51.414 --> 09:53.934
If I'm not there, what's everyone going to eat?

164
09:53.959 --> 09:56.195
Besides, I'd totally outshine all the models.

165
09:57.712 --> 10:03.425
Belle, are the models' and celebrities' outfits all set?

166
10:03.450 --> 10:07.241
Everything's on track. Fahsai is coming this afternoon to help.

167
10:07.851 --> 10:10.562
Fahsai? She's coming this afternoon?

168
10:10.689 --> 10:13.503
- Yes. - Hmm. That's too bad.

169
10:13.528 --> 10:18.088
Pro Vee and I have to go check out the golf gear

170
10:18.113 --> 10:20.519
our sponsors are providing for the event.

171
10:25.274 --> 10:29.118
Unless you'd rather stay and help Fahsai?

172
10:29.143 --> 10:30.888
I can go alone.

173
10:33.027 --> 10:34.774
Whatever you say, Miss Nana.

174
10:38.878 --> 10:42.448
All right, everyone. Ready for our first rehearsal?

175
10:42.473 --> 10:44.164
- Ready! - Ready!

176
10:44.252 --> 10:46.797
Hmm? What's with that energy?

177
10:46.822 --> 10:48.487
I know you can do this.

178
10:48.512 --> 10:50.126
Have a little confidence in yourselves.

179
10:50.150 --> 10:52.356
Come on! Let's hear some energy. Ready?

180
10:52.570 --> 10:54.237
- Ready! - Ready!

181
10:59.673 --> 11:03.080
♪ Everyone can tell by the way you stare ♪

182
11:03.818 --> 11:05.669
♪ Sneaking little looks when I'm unaware ♪

183
11:05.694 --> 11:09.189
♪ It's plain to see ♪

184
11:09.571 --> 11:11.468
♪ I know exactly what you think of me ♪

185
11:11.493 --> 11:14.662
♪ First to watch my stories every time ♪

186
11:15.386 --> 11:17.259
♪ You remember every fave of mine ♪

187
11:17.284 --> 11:20.611
♪ Everywhere I go, you're by my side ♪

188
11:21.052 --> 11:23.052
♪ Don't tell me there's nothing on your mind ♪

189
11:23.077 --> 11:25.849
♪ So when are you gonna say the words? ♪

190
11:25.874 --> 11:28.034
♪ Don't keep me waiting till it hurts ♪

191
11:28.059 --> 11:30.513
♪ The way you act, I know you're into me ♪

192
11:30.538 --> 11:33.516
♪ That racing heart gives you away so easily ♪

193
11:33.541 --> 11:37.225
♪ But I'll play clueless, just wait and see ♪

194
11:37.250 --> 11:39.250
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

195
11:41.258 --> 11:43.258
So handsome!

196
11:45.714 --> 11:49.812
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

197
11:50.663 --> 11:53.244
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

198
11:53.269 --> 11:56.596
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

199
11:56.621 --> 12:00.310
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

200
12:00.335 --> 12:03.097
Gorgeous!

201
12:06.419 --> 12:07.729
Beautiful.

202
12:16.416 --> 12:17.939
Let's put on a face mask

203
12:17.964 --> 12:19.566
so you'll look gorgeous on the big day.

204
12:19.654 --> 12:21.812
No. I don't like them. They're all sticky.

205
12:34.982 --> 12:37.905
This one's not sticky. Don't be difficult.

206
12:37.930 --> 12:40.508
I don't want you to be the odd one out on the catwalk.

207
12:41.134 --> 12:43.624
Do I look that bad to you?

208
12:45.070 --> 12:47.820
To me, you're beautiful.

209
12:47.845 --> 12:51.720
But I want everyone else to notice how beautiful you are too.

210
12:53.527 --> 12:55.439
Aren't you afraid someone might hit on me?

211
12:56.757 --> 12:59.465
I hope they do. Then I'll know you're really beautiful,

212
12:59.490 --> 13:00.961
and it's not just me who thinks so.

213
13:01.381 --> 13:03.762
If someone really does hit on me,

214
13:04.361 --> 13:05.919
don't regret it later.

215
13:06.792 --> 13:11.087
You had first dibs and didn't make your move.

216
13:12.551 --> 13:14.233
I don't make the first move.

217
13:15.100 --> 13:18.142
When it's the right person, one look is enough.

218
13:18.564 --> 13:22.861
No need for words. No need to waste time flirting.

219
13:29.724 --> 13:31.109
Do you know now?

220
13:32.962 --> 13:37.511
No. You still look a little unsure, Pro Jin.

221
13:44.236 --> 13:47.950
How about now? Is that clear enough?

222
13:53.492 --> 13:54.539
Now do you know?

223
14:22.064 --> 14:23.877
Your skin is so smooth.

224
14:27.248 --> 14:31.570
And this nose... under the catwalk lights,

225
14:32.205 --> 14:33.879
it'll stand out even more.

226
14:36.798 --> 14:42.269
When you're blessed with beauty, you've got to take care of it.

227
14:56.146 --> 14:57.178
All done.

228
14:57.853 --> 14:59.154
Here. Let me do yours.

229
14:59.543 --> 15:02.466
It's okay. I prefer doing it myself.

230
15:03.330 --> 15:06.477
All right. Leave it on for 20 minutes, then rinse it off.

231
15:54.798 --> 15:57.559
I saw your light was still on, so I figured you were awake.

232
15:58.695 --> 15:59.735
Here.

233
16:02.486 --> 16:03.913
Thanks.

234
16:04.128 --> 16:07.191
I just want to make absolutely sure nothing goes wrong tomorrow.

235
16:09.450 --> 16:12.859
You can't keep losing sleep. You'll wear yourself out.

236
16:13.473 --> 16:16.499
I'm fine. I just want to check one more thing.

237
16:16.524 --> 16:18.382
You've checked it at least ten times.

238
16:18.407 --> 16:20.129
Don't you have to get up early tomorrow?

239
16:20.153 --> 16:23.210
- Very early. - Then go to bed.

240
16:24.023 --> 16:26.982
I won't be able to sleep. I'm too excited.

241
16:27.007 --> 16:29.607
I can't wait to see how everything turns out tomorrow.

242
16:30.188 --> 16:34.676
It'll be great. You've personally overseen every detail.

243
16:35.161 --> 16:38.744
But honestly, I'm a little nervous too.

244
16:38.990 --> 16:41.262
I'm worried I'll miss this or forget that.

245
16:41.287 --> 16:43.583
Hmm... come here.

246
16:57.651 --> 16:59.976
Vee... is this really okay?

247
17:00.001 --> 17:02.702
I'm not ready yet. And tomorrow...

248
17:02.727 --> 17:04.487
What do you think I'm going to do?

249
17:05.033 --> 17:06.042
Well...

250
17:07.519 --> 17:10.830
- Well... - Well, what?

251
17:12.130 --> 17:17.179
I mean a moment like this, just the two of us...

252
17:24.427 --> 17:25.983
Vee...

253
17:31.132 --> 17:33.117
- Go to sleep. - Hmm?

254
17:33.268 --> 17:35.724
- I brought you here to sleep. - Oh?

255
17:43.844 --> 17:45.718
Come here. I'll massage your hands.

256
17:53.251 --> 17:54.626
That feels so good.

257
17:57.008 --> 18:00.241
When I was little, I'd practice every day before a tournament.

258
18:00.266 --> 18:02.935
Mom would do this whenever I couldn't sleep.

259
18:03.439 --> 18:04.453
Feel better?

260
18:06.088 --> 18:07.090
Much better.

261
18:25.532 --> 18:26.590
Nana?

262
18:30.180 --> 18:31.347
That was fast.

263
18:41.239 --> 18:42.284
Sweet dreams.

264
18:58.884 --> 19:00.926
Jeab, put the flowers right here, please.

265
19:03.150 --> 19:04.484
And this one over here.

266
19:09.570 --> 19:10.726
Thank you so much.

267
19:17.811 --> 19:21.086
- How's everything going? - Everything's ready.

268
19:27.136 --> 19:30.770
Pro Vee, let me check everything for you.

269
19:32.678 --> 19:35.301
Does this fit okay? You look gorgeous.

270
19:35.326 --> 19:37.579
Nana, could you come over here?

271
19:40.203 --> 19:43.910
Could you give me one final check? Just to be safe.

272
19:48.489 --> 19:53.825
Fahsai, could you go double-check that area... over there?

273
19:55.171 --> 19:57.568
Way over there. Could you do that for me?

274
19:58.193 --> 20:00.793
- Me? - Mm-hmm. Please?

275
20:01.495 --> 20:03.763
- Love you. - That's so far!

276
20:08.542 --> 20:10.567
Everything looks fine, Vee.

277
20:10.925 --> 20:14.767
Maybe I just needed a little encouragement. I'm nervous.

278
20:15.378 --> 20:18.232
What are you nervous about? This is our golf course.

279
20:18.257 --> 20:20.771
You know every inch of it better than anyone.

280
20:21.086 --> 20:22.674
You've got this.

281
20:24.550 --> 20:28.002
Everyone, fifteen minutes! Are we ready?

282
20:28.541 --> 20:30.220
- No! - Not ready!

283
20:31.533 --> 20:33.134
Well, I'm ready!

284
20:33.159 --> 20:36.432
I had my Douyin makeup done extra glamorous.

285
20:39.747 --> 20:43.193
- I'm nervous, Nana. - What is everyone so scared of?

286
20:44.134 --> 20:47.914
Come on. Let's put our hands in and get some energy going.

287
20:47.939 --> 20:50.527
- Come on, gather around... - So this is where everyone is.

288
20:50.552 --> 20:53.529
- Sir! - Dad? What are you doing here?

289
20:53.554 --> 20:56.612
Our VVIP belongs in the front row over there!

290
20:56.637 --> 20:58.919
Eh? I came to cheer you on.

291
20:58.944 --> 21:02.644
Aww, that's so sweet. Come give us a boost too, Dad.

292
21:02.669 --> 21:04.669
A boost? How?

293
21:05.854 --> 21:08.774
All right, everyone. Vive la vie!

294
21:08.799 --> 21:09.952
Vive la what-the-what?

295
21:09.976 --> 21:12.421
Yes! One more time. One, two, three!

296
21:12.446 --> 21:15.249
- Vive la vie! - Vive la vie!

297
21:17.171 --> 21:22.523
Oh, I feel it now! That's a boost!

298
21:22.548 --> 21:24.803
- Looking handsome today. - Thank you, Miss.

299
21:49.019 --> 21:51.964
♪ Say it, say it. Say "You love me." ♪

300
21:51.989 --> 21:54.930
♪ Call me, call me. Call me "Baby." ♪

301
22:01.040 --> 22:03.716
♪ So when are you gonna say the words? ♪

302
22:03.741 --> 22:06.559
♪ Just one more little try, my dear ♪

303
22:06.584 --> 22:09.434
♪ Or we'll be wasting one whole year ♪

304
22:09.459 --> 22:11.459
♪ Don't keep me waiting till it hurts ♪

305
22:11.484 --> 22:14.327
♪ The way you act, I know you're into me ♪

306
22:14.352 --> 22:17.218
♪ That racing heart gives you away so easily ♪

307
22:17.243 --> 22:21.023
♪ But I'll play clueless, just wait and see ♪

308
22:21.048 --> 22:23.048
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

309
22:23.073 --> 22:25.815
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

310
22:25.840 --> 22:29.397
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

311
22:29.422 --> 22:33.786
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

312
22:33.811 --> 22:35.811
♪ Or should I be the one to call your bluff? ♪

313
22:35.836 --> 22:38.471
♪ Say it, say it. Say "You love me." ♪

314
22:38.496 --> 22:41.426
♪ Call me, call me. Call me "Baby." ♪

315
22:46.740 --> 22:49.187
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

316
22:49.212 --> 22:52.691
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

317
22:52.716 --> 22:57.409
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

318
22:57.434 --> 22:59.434
♪ Or should I be the one to call your bluff? ♪

319
23:01.691 --> 23:05.157
That was amazing! Thank you so much, everyone.

320
23:05.990 --> 23:07.263
You did great, sweetheart.

321
23:15.288 --> 23:19.108
- You did so well. - Amazing.

322
23:22.031 --> 23:24.037
Thank you all so much.

323
23:24.062 --> 23:27.068
This wouldn't have turned out half as well without all of you.

324
23:27.093 --> 23:30.128
It turned out even better than I imagined.

325
23:30.473 --> 23:32.768
We had over ten thousand viewers on the livestream.

326
23:32.793 --> 23:34.484
Our highest ever.

327
23:35.905 --> 23:39.073
Online is one thing, but seeing everyone in person...

328
23:39.098 --> 23:43.411
You're all gorgeous. I'm seriously impressed.

329
23:46.171 --> 23:48.362
At first, all I could think about was

330
23:48.387 --> 23:51.387
how to bring this course back to life.

331
23:51.412 --> 23:55.363
But today I realized we don't just have a beautiful course.

332
23:55.388 --> 23:57.316
We also have talented,

333
23:57.341 --> 23:59.669
forward-thinking people ready to move forward together.

334
23:59.694 --> 24:02.945
That's because you made us believe in ourselves, Miss Nana.

335
24:02.970 --> 24:05.740
- Right, everyone? - Absolutely!

336
24:05.978 --> 24:07.434
Thank you. I really mean it.

337
24:07.459 --> 24:12.228
And we've still got a lot more fun things ahead of us.

338
24:12.253 --> 24:13.660
So let's keep going together.

339
24:15.207 --> 24:19.466
Vive la vie! Vive la vie!

340
24:19.491 --> 24:26.600
Allez! Allez!

341
24:26.625 --> 24:33.378
Allez! Allez!

342
24:33.402 --> 24:36.597
Allez! Allez!

343
24:36.622 --> 24:39.147
Nana, are you okay?

344
24:40.266 --> 24:43.402
I'm fine.

345
24:46.155 --> 24:48.362
- Hey! - Miss Nana!

346
24:48.387 --> 24:50.477
- Nana! - Call an ambulance!

347
24:50.502 --> 24:54.079
- Anyone have smelling salts? - Any smelling salts?

348
24:54.104 --> 24:56.503
Don't crowd her. Give her some space.

349
25:07.122 --> 25:09.659
Hey, she's awake!

350
25:18.467 --> 25:22.735
I'm in the hospital, right? What happened?

351
25:23.430 --> 25:25.893
You were talking to me, then suddenly you just fainted.

352
25:26.242 --> 25:27.560
You scared all of us.

353
25:28.253 --> 25:31.041
Seriously. You know what I thought?

354
25:31.066 --> 25:33.741
I thought this was like one of those dramas

355
25:33.766 --> 25:35.344
where someone suddenly collapses

356
25:35.368 --> 25:39.004
because they've been secretly hiding some terrible illness

357
25:39.029 --> 25:40.312
and never told anyone.

358
25:40.439 --> 25:41.931
Enough with the drama, Queen.

359
25:41.956 --> 25:44.565
The doctor said Nana just hasn't been resting enough.

360
25:44.590 --> 25:46.112
She's just exhausted.

361
25:48.297 --> 25:50.705
You can't keep pushing yourself this hard.

362
25:50.730 --> 25:52.937
You need to take care of yourself too.

363
25:53.507 --> 25:57.188
Just remember, you have me here to handle things,

364
25:57.213 --> 26:01.489
and everyone at Goodview is always here to support you.

365
26:07.303 --> 26:10.455
Hello? What game are you talking about?

366
26:10.844 --> 26:13.352
I'm at the hospital. I'm not playing tonight.

367
26:18.134 --> 26:20.216
My friends want me to play. One sec.

368
26:25.972 --> 26:27.876
No, I'm not playing. I'm at the hospital.

369
26:32.054 --> 26:34.177
- Oh, Mr. Sanchai. - Doctor. Hello.

370
26:34.202 --> 26:36.018
Hello. What brings you here today?

371
26:36.043 --> 26:39.268
My daughter overworked herself and fainted,

372
26:39.293 --> 26:41.268
so she's staying here for a couple of days.

373
26:41.293 --> 26:45.630
I see. And what about your chemotherapy plan?

374
26:46.362 --> 26:48.713
Have you decided when you'd like to start?

375
26:54.571 --> 26:56.737
I haven't really decided yet.

376
26:57.158 --> 26:59.158
I'll get back to you as soon as I can.

377
27:00.690 --> 27:02.745
All right. But don't wait too long.

378
27:02.770 --> 27:04.404
It could spread further.

379
27:06.049 --> 27:08.269
- Understood. Thank you, Doctor. - Excuse me, then.

380
27:18.091 --> 27:21.683
Chemo? Dad has cancer?

381
27:29.571 --> 27:32.447
Her vitals are normal. No fever or other symptoms.

382
27:32.472 --> 27:35.501
She may just be experiencing fatigue, as the doctor mentioned.

383
27:35.526 --> 27:37.526
Okay. Thank you very much.

384
27:44.754 --> 27:45.825
You're okay now, dear.

385
27:46.667 --> 27:48.411
Since you're already in the hospital,

386
27:48.435 --> 27:51.564
why don't you get a full checkup while you're here?

387
27:55.682 --> 27:58.254
He's right, Miss Nana. Your health is important.

388
27:58.279 --> 28:02.105
I may look like a little pig, but I'm a very healthy pig.

389
28:03.339 --> 28:05.324
I'm really fine.

390
28:05.686 --> 28:07.598
Get checked anyway.

391
28:07.623 --> 28:09.979
You've still got plenty of projects ahead of you.

392
28:14.613 --> 28:15.686
All right.

393
28:16.227 --> 28:19.116
Good. Now get some rest.

394
28:20.273 --> 28:23.168
If there's nothing else, we should all head home

395
28:23.193 --> 28:24.645
so Nana can get some proper rest.

396
28:24.670 --> 28:26.497
Oh, wait, sir...

397
28:26.734 --> 28:30.156
Isn't anyone staying overnight with her?

398
28:30.181 --> 28:32.967
It's okay. Everyone must be exhausted already.

399
28:32.992 --> 28:39.195
Oh, no, Miss Nana! Hospitals have ghosts, you know.

400
28:39.220 --> 28:41.045
Haven't you heard all those scary stories

401
28:41.070 --> 28:43.103
about ghosts under hospital beds?

402
28:43.128 --> 28:45.045
You'll never get any sleep.

403
28:46.714 --> 28:49.953
Then can you stay with Nana, Chef Queen?

404
28:50.360 --> 28:51.678
- Chef Queen... Me? - Yes.

405
28:52.538 --> 28:57.127
I mean, I could... but around two in the morning,

406
28:57.152 --> 28:59.740
I tend to wake up and snore like this.

407
28:59.765 --> 29:02.891
Yes, exactly like this.

408
29:03.066 --> 29:07.073
You wouldn't get any rest at all. So I'm definitely not suitable.

409
29:07.098 --> 29:09.782
Then I'll stay with Miss Nana.

410
29:10.757 --> 29:13.687
Belle, you have a mountain of paperwork waiting.

411
29:13.712 --> 29:15.722
With Miss Nana away,

412
29:15.747 --> 29:17.992
you really should stay and take care of all that.

413
29:19.058 --> 29:21.272
Oh... right. That's true.

414
29:22.826 --> 29:24.190
Right, Miss Nana?

415
29:25.627 --> 29:28.040
Uh... yes.

416
29:28.470 --> 29:30.214
See? Belle really isn't the right person.

417
29:30.239 --> 29:31.255
Go get some work done.

418
29:32.660 --> 29:35.050
Gus, can you stay with your sister tonight?

419
29:35.075 --> 29:38.871
Gus! Don't you have work at the course?

420
29:39.648 --> 29:42.017
And besides, a man and a woman, sharing a bathroom?

421
29:42.042 --> 29:44.812
That'd be awkward.

422
29:44.837 --> 29:46.338
Oh, just go home!

423
29:46.363 --> 29:48.554
Then I'll hire a private nurse to stay with Nana.

424
29:48.579 --> 29:51.987
Oh, no, Sir. You can't just use any nurse on duty.

425
29:52.012 --> 29:54.245
What's going on? No one I suggest is good enough.

426
29:54.270 --> 29:56.372
Then I'll stay with Nana tonight.

427
29:56.397 --> 29:58.270
Oh! Now that makes sense.

428
29:58.517 --> 30:01.992
See? She's the perfect choice.

429
30:07.771 --> 30:11.020
Perfect! Pro Vee, you're free tonight, right?

430
30:11.045 --> 30:12.064
I am.

431
30:13.129 --> 30:15.910
Don't worry, Sir. They can take care of each other.

432
30:15.935 --> 30:20.216
Now, why don't we all head home?

433
30:21.503 --> 30:22.753
After you, Sir.

434
30:23.721 --> 30:27.049
I'll have the club driver bring some clothes over for you.

435
30:27.074 --> 30:28.096
Thank you.

436
30:32.363 --> 30:34.011
Get some rest, dear, okay?

437
30:35.789 --> 30:37.051
Thank you, Pro Vee.

438
30:38.463 --> 30:41.739
We should get going, Sir. After you.

439
30:41.764 --> 30:42.947
Let's go.

440
30:48.089 --> 30:49.289
After you, Sir.

441
30:54.123 --> 30:55.618
This way, please.

442
31:06.248 --> 31:07.436
Thank you.

443
31:14.840 --> 31:18.435
- I'll be heading off, then. - I'll go with you.

444
31:20.226 --> 31:23.394
I'll get going too, Sir. Good night.

445
31:23.419 --> 31:25.085
- Get home safely. - I will.

446
31:26.713 --> 31:28.338
- Dad. - What is it?

447
31:29.299 --> 31:31.703
You really should get a health checkup sometime.

448
31:32.743 --> 31:33.780
Why?

449
31:35.463 --> 31:38.042
I'm perfectly healthy. Why would I need a checkup?

450
31:40.354 --> 31:41.479
Are you sure, Dad?

451
31:42.409 --> 31:44.386
Do I look unhealthy to you?

452
31:44.411 --> 31:46.872
I play golf every single day.

453
31:46.897 --> 31:50.732
I can still drive the ball 300 yards.

454
31:50.830 --> 31:52.791
How could I possibly look sick?

455
31:52.816 --> 31:55.068
What about you? Don't you have class tomorrow?

456
31:58.158 --> 31:59.400
Come on. Let's go home.

457
32:37.255 --> 32:38.452
Where are you going?

458
32:40.549 --> 32:42.098
To the bathroom.

459
32:42.217 --> 32:43.439
I'll take you.

460
32:43.464 --> 32:45.907
It's okay. I can go by myself.

461
32:46.437 --> 32:49.794
What if you faint again? Let me help you.

462
32:55.390 --> 32:57.216
Don't lock the bathroom door.

463
32:58.107 --> 32:59.160
Why not?

464
32:59.184 --> 33:02.506
In case you faint or fall, so I can get to you right away.

465
33:06.599 --> 33:11.182
Vee, you don't have to stand that close to the door.

466
33:11.767 --> 33:13.139
I'm not going to peek.

467
33:13.385 --> 33:16.473
It's not about peeking. It's about...

468
33:17.828 --> 33:18.875
the sound.

469
33:20.225 --> 33:23.996
Then I'll turn the music up so you won't feel embarrassed.

470
33:45.191 --> 33:47.545
All done? Come on, I'll help you.

471
34:08.257 --> 34:09.347
Go to sleep.

472
34:15.868 --> 34:17.510
Will you massage my hands?

473
34:18.637 --> 34:19.653
Hmm?

474
34:20.637 --> 34:21.900
Like you did last night.

475
34:30.373 --> 34:31.373
Come here.

476
34:33.958 --> 34:38.418
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

477
34:39.107 --> 34:44.141
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

478
34:44.300 --> 34:48.693
♪ Together, we'll race toward the line ♪

479
34:49.403 --> 34:53.745
♪ Chasing the dream that's yours and mine ♪

480
34:54.432 --> 34:59.609
♪ In the end, I know we'll make it there ♪

481
34:59.634 --> 35:03.939
♪ Just one rule for you and me to share ♪

482
35:04.601 --> 35:07.833
♪ Promise you'll stay close to me ♪

483
35:07.858 --> 35:10.313
♪ Hold me in your arms so tenderly ♪

484
35:10.338 --> 35:15.855
♪ I've never bowed to anyone in sight ♪

485
35:15.880 --> 35:18.956
♪ But for you, I'd surrender without a fight ♪

486
35:18.981 --> 35:23.348
♪ Just take my hand and hold it tight ♪

487
35:23.607 --> 35:25.024
Let me wipe your mouth.

488
35:25.484 --> 35:27.484
Miss Nana, about the fashion...

489
35:31.183 --> 35:32.501
Come in, Belle.

490
35:33.375 --> 35:36.303
I feel like I came at a bad time.

491
35:37.773 --> 35:39.008
Want some water?

492
35:42.139 --> 35:43.163
Thank you.

493
35:47.867 --> 35:50.946
- Go ahead. - What about the fashion show?

494
35:51.456 --> 35:55.349
I had a wrap-up meeting with the event team yesterday,

495
35:55.374 --> 35:57.883
and the response has been amazing.

496
35:58.139 --> 36:00.657
Four or five clients called this morning

497
36:00.682 --> 36:03.406
asking about renting our course for their own events.

498
36:03.674 --> 36:06.869
And both of our pros have started getting job offers too.

499
36:06.894 --> 36:10.986
People have been calling to ask their rates for product reviews.

500
36:11.910 --> 36:13.315
You did it.

501
36:13.438 --> 36:17.222
Our course is becoming more than just a place to play golf.

502
36:17.346 --> 36:19.744
Oh, and I don't know if it's a coincidence,

503
36:19.769 --> 36:21.642
but four of your students

504
36:21.667 --> 36:24.136
have already renewed their lesson packages.

505
36:24.161 --> 36:26.462
And people have been asking

506
36:26.487 --> 36:28.720
about the collection from yesterday's show too.

507
36:28.745 --> 36:30.467
They want to know where they can buy it.

508
36:31.650 --> 36:34.710
Then why don't we start taking orders through our pro shop?

509
36:40.134 --> 36:41.593
- Hello. - Hello.

510
36:42.022 --> 36:44.664
- How are you feeling? - Back to normal.

511
36:44.689 --> 36:46.498
Can I leave the hospital yet?

512
36:46.523 --> 36:48.523
I really want to get back to work.

513
36:48.815 --> 36:50.672
Overall, you look fine.

514
36:50.969 --> 36:53.366
But let's wait for your checkup results first.

515
36:53.517 --> 36:56.549
If everything looks good, you can go home this afternoon.

516
36:57.057 --> 36:59.354
- Okay. - Thank you.

517
36:59.386 --> 37:00.396
Thank you, Doctor.

518
37:03.412 --> 37:06.274
Belle, can you look after Nana for me?

519
37:06.299 --> 37:09.747
I have lessons this afternoon, but I'll come back this evening.

520
37:09.940 --> 37:11.560
Of course. Don't worry.

521
37:12.662 --> 37:13.940
I'll be back.

522
37:21.487 --> 37:24.882
Look at this. Goodview's fashion show yesterday.

523
37:25.495 --> 37:27.201
People were checking in nonstop.

524
37:28.734 --> 37:30.686
It's probably just a passing trend.

525
37:30.711 --> 37:31.741
It'll die down soon.

526
37:32.130 --> 37:34.622
Then start putting that plan of yours into action.

527
37:35.142 --> 37:37.166
Stop talking and prove yourself.

528
37:37.191 --> 37:40.682
Don't make me think it's no coincidence

529
37:40.877 --> 37:44.140
that Goodview has only gotten better since you left.

530
37:44.286 --> 37:45.302
Ms. Yupadee.

531
37:47.448 --> 37:48.776
Isn't that a little harsh?

532
37:49.537 --> 37:50.965
I can be much harsher.

533
37:51.992 --> 37:57.623
Especially if I start thinking I made a mistake hiring you.

534
37:59.982 --> 38:01.709
You won't regret hiring me.

535
38:04.234 --> 38:07.327
Then show me this plan you keep talking about.

536
38:10.868 --> 38:11.876
Yes.

537
38:13.066 --> 38:15.474
You'll be wanting to give me a raise soon enough.

538
38:30.724 --> 38:32.082
Vee, are you taking me...

539
38:32.545 --> 38:35.457
- Hi! - Home...

540
38:36.376 --> 38:37.970
Oh. Fahsai.

541
38:37.995 --> 38:40.352
How are you? I ran into Pro Vee at the course,

542
38:40.377 --> 38:42.407
so I tagged along to see you.

543
38:42.615 --> 38:45.216
I'm fine. The doctor said I just haven't been resting enough.

544
38:45.534 --> 38:48.474
That's what I thought. You're usually so healthy.

545
38:48.499 --> 38:55.007
I brought you some shrimp congee. This place is amazing.

546
38:57.003 --> 39:01.070
- Thanks. - But Nana's allergic to shrimp.

547
39:04.594 --> 39:08.362
Really? I had no idea.

548
39:11.463 --> 39:12.868
You remembered.

549
39:17.471 --> 39:20.331
Oh, you knew about that too, Pro Vee?

550
39:20.489 --> 39:22.990
She's been allergic since she was little.

551
39:23.872 --> 39:28.710
Oh, so you and Nana have known each other since childhood?

552
39:32.391 --> 39:34.534
I'm such a terrible friend.

553
39:34.559 --> 39:37.653
I don't pay attention to anything.

554
39:37.955 --> 39:39.447
It's okay, Fahsai.

555
39:39.472 --> 39:41.472
And now I bought this for nothing.

556
39:42.090 --> 39:45.587
It's fine. We can give it to one of the nurses.

557
39:45.816 --> 39:47.112
That works.

558
39:47.793 --> 39:51.958
Oh, Nana, did you know yesterday's fashion show

559
39:51.983 --> 39:57.441
was all over fashion pages, sports pages, and society news?

560
39:58.123 --> 40:01.454
Thanks for helping as my consultant, Fahsai.

561
40:01.874 --> 40:05.893
Anytime. Maybe you can repay me

562
40:05.918 --> 40:09.107
with free golf lessons from Vee.

563
40:09.732 --> 40:12.765
I've only had a few lessons with you so far.

564
40:12.790 --> 40:14.887
Your schedule is packed.

565
40:14.912 --> 40:17.468
Actually, I was just about to tell you

566
40:17.493 --> 40:20.286
that another pro will take over your remaining lessons.

567
40:20.475 --> 40:23.040
What? Why?

568
40:23.349 --> 40:27.312
My schedule got too complicated, so they've already redone it.

569
40:27.337 --> 40:29.646
They've assigned you another pro too,

570
40:29.671 --> 40:31.696
so your lessons won't be interrupted.

571
40:31.720 --> 40:34.176
But I want to learn from you.

572
40:34.201 --> 40:38.003
All the pros are excellent. They all meet the same standards.

573
40:38.062 --> 40:39.943
It doesn't matter which pro you learn from.

574
40:39.968 --> 40:41.968
It does matter. I...

575
40:43.922 --> 40:45.161
Excuse me.

576
40:51.398 --> 40:54.353
The doctor says you can go home now.

577
41:11.629 --> 41:13.351
You've taken your before-meal meds.

578
41:13.375 --> 41:15.933
Now eat, then take the after-meal ones.

579
41:16.324 --> 41:20.509
I had Chef Queen make you tofu soup with minced pork.

580
41:20.534 --> 41:22.806
When I was little and recovering from a fever,

581
41:22.831 --> 41:26.318
so I'd get better faster.

582
41:26.810 --> 41:28.318
It looks delicious.

583
41:29.995 --> 41:32.059
Speaking of your mom,

584
41:32.084 --> 41:35.282
I really want to go back and finish the pot we made.

585
41:36.368 --> 41:39.529
Sure. Let's go see Mom on my next day off.

586
41:39.632 --> 41:45.003
But my hands still feel so weak right now. What should I do?

587
41:45.028 --> 41:50.215
Oh, sounds like someone needs another night in the hospital.

588
41:51.822 --> 41:56.928
Vee, I just want you to feed me. That's all.

589
41:57.407 --> 41:59.844
Then just say so. Go on.

590
42:00.306 --> 42:05.936
Pretty Vee... please feed me. Please?

591
42:06.890 --> 42:08.767
See? That wasn't so hard.

592
42:09.236 --> 42:13.229
Remember, if you want something from me, just say it straight.

593
42:41.278 --> 42:42.549
It's so good.

594
43:15.843 --> 43:19.689
With all our recent projects, including the fashion show,

595
43:19.714 --> 43:22.726
we've created a lot of buzz around the course.

596
43:23.337 --> 43:28.613
We've also brought in more non-golfers visit a golf course.

597
43:29.001 --> 43:32.351
So I think we need to build on that

598
43:32.376 --> 43:34.280
and keep Goodview in people's minds.

599
43:34.348 --> 43:37.738
From now on, we'll each create fun content for the course

600
43:37.763 --> 43:39.703
based on our strengths.

601
43:39.727 --> 43:42.347
And every month, I'll give bonuses

602
43:42.372 --> 43:45.284
to the top five people with the most views.

603
43:45.368 --> 43:49.212
I love it. But I have no idea what to make.

604
43:49.795 --> 43:53.898
Food, obviously. Make food content.

605
43:56.356 --> 43:59.423
Everyone!

606
43:59.448 --> 44:02.291
I'm sure a lot of you have already fallen in love

607
44:02.316 --> 44:04.783
with my cooking at Goodview.

608
44:05.113 --> 44:07.892
Birdie Bites!

609
44:07.917 --> 44:11.054
Today, I'm teaching you something super easy.

610
44:11.079 --> 44:13.307
If you can make it, make it. If you can eat it, eat it.

611
44:13.332 --> 44:14.725
If not, throw it away!

612
44:14.750 --> 44:16.565
Before every round,

613
44:16.590 --> 44:20.707
you should always warm up first. Let's start with this stretch.

614
44:20.974 --> 44:23.695
Rest the golf club across the back of your shoulders.

615
44:23.720 --> 44:25.434
Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart,

616
44:25.459 --> 44:27.459
then rotate your torso to the left.

617
44:29.430 --> 44:31.372
Then rotate to the right.

618
44:33.285 --> 44:35.158
This helps stretch your spine.

619
44:36.019 --> 44:38.172
Give it a try at home.

620
44:40.872 --> 44:43.743
Hi, everyone. Welcome to Golf by the Green.

621
44:43.768 --> 44:47.791
Today, I'm taking you to see the toughest hole on our course.

622
44:47.816 --> 44:52.487
It's a par-5 island hole, the longest on the course,

623
44:52.512 --> 44:54.547
and the windiest, too.

624
44:54.968 --> 44:56.721
Hi, everyone. On today's Caddie Secrets,

625
44:56.746 --> 44:58.584
I'll show you how to read a green,

626
44:58.608 --> 45:01.603
the way even some pros have to ask their caddies about.

627
45:01.628 --> 45:04.843
I'll show you what to look for before making your shot.

628
45:16.748 --> 45:19.501
Your course is really making a name for itself these days.

629
45:19.526 --> 45:20.674
Seen the news?

630
45:20.769 --> 45:24.371
Goodview clips keep popping up on my phone every day.

631
45:25.589 --> 45:30.418
Seriously. My wife even knows all your caddies by name now.

632
45:30.434 --> 45:32.116
She even makes me book them for her.

633
45:32.141 --> 45:35.003
- That's dangerous. - Tell me about it.

634
45:35.028 --> 45:36.193
You'd better watch out.

635
45:36.218 --> 45:38.658
Your daughter's really something.

636
45:38.683 --> 45:40.436
Didn't you say she studied fashion?

637
45:40.461 --> 45:42.000
Yeah, she graduated in fashion.

638
45:42.868 --> 45:45.672
She takes after her old man in every way.

639
45:45.697 --> 45:47.809
- She's just like me. - That's good.

640
45:47.834 --> 45:50.820
Once she sets her mind on something, she never lets go.

641
45:50.845 --> 45:54.023
Then I guess you don't have to worry anymore.

642
45:54.048 --> 45:56.549
You thought it was done for, and now it's bouncing right back.

643
45:56.668 --> 45:58.804
- Yeah. - Come on.

644
45:58.829 --> 46:01.456
Guys our age need to know when to step aside

645
46:01.481 --> 46:03.734
and let our kids take over.

646
46:05.999 --> 46:11.086
Hey, I ran into Wut last week. He said he's beaten cancer.

647
46:11.315 --> 46:13.672
Cancer can actually be cured?

648
46:13.696 --> 46:16.476
Of course. Doctors are amazing these days.

649
46:16.501 --> 46:18.255
Speaking of which,

650
46:18.280 --> 46:21.199
when are you starting that chemo your doctor recommended?

651
46:21.556 --> 46:23.316
The longer you wait, the worse it could get

652
46:23.341 --> 46:25.341
and become harder to treat.

653
46:28.185 --> 46:31.362
My doctor wants me to start treatment right away, too.

654
46:33.313 --> 46:35.646
I just need a little more time to come to terms with it.

655
46:36.559 --> 46:39.638
Hey, no matter how much money you have...

656
46:40.469 --> 46:42.072
If something happens to you,

657
46:42.097 --> 46:44.097
you won't even be around to spend all that money.

658
46:44.654 --> 46:47.802
- Is that a warning or a curse? - Maybe both.

659
46:49.772 --> 46:54.630
Seriously, though, you should tell your kids about it.

660
46:57.208 --> 46:58.217
Yeah.

661
47:09.349 --> 47:10.389
Hi, Mom.

662
47:10.414 --> 47:11.842
- Hello, Aunt Sinee. - Hello, dear.

663
47:11.867 --> 47:15.344
- You're feeling better now? - I'm all better.

664
47:15.369 --> 47:16.895
Thank you for worrying about me.

665
47:16.920 --> 47:19.135
Want to come see the vase you made last time?

666
47:19.160 --> 47:21.918
I've already fired it. You can paint it today.

667
47:22.546 --> 47:24.419
- Let's go. - Okay.

668
47:30.250 --> 47:34.095
It looks kind of weird. It's not as pretty as your other pieces.

669
47:35.143 --> 47:37.347
It matches your personality.

670
47:38.291 --> 47:39.960
Are you saying I'm weird?

671
47:39.985 --> 47:45.512
Oh, Vee probably means you have your own unique style.

672
47:46.043 --> 47:47.075
Right?

673
47:48.289 --> 47:50.263
- Yes, Mom. - Mm-hmm.

674
47:51.287 --> 47:54.644
I've got the paints ready. You can start whenever you like.

675
47:54.669 --> 47:56.583
- Okay. - Vee, help her out.

676
47:56.608 --> 47:59.203
- Sure. - Take your time.

677
48:09.030 --> 48:11.371
First, put on one or two base coats.

678
48:11.396 --> 48:12.863
Then you can add the actual color.

679
48:14.182 --> 48:16.659
Like putting on primer before makeup.

680
48:16.684 --> 48:20.596
Yeah, pretty much. Like this.

681
48:25.745 --> 48:27.113
Like this.

682
48:30.575 --> 48:32.427
- Want to try? - Sure.

683
48:35.686 --> 48:39.451
Just brush it on. That's it.

684
48:52.835 --> 48:54.135
Is it pretty, Vee?

685
48:56.901 --> 48:57.980
Pretty.

686
48:58.583 --> 49:01.880
This or me? Which one's prettier?

687
49:02.563 --> 49:04.563
What do you want me to say?

688
49:05.442 --> 49:09.231
That your Nana is the prettiest of all.

689
49:11.468 --> 49:17.106
My Nana is... the cringiest of all.

690
49:17.361 --> 49:20.055
Cringiest? What does that mean?

691
49:20.080 --> 49:24.406
It means cute. Super cute.

692
49:24.876 --> 49:30.005
I don't think so. Don't lie. Tell me what it really means.

693
49:30.030 --> 49:32.664
It means you're pretty, cute,

694
49:32.689 --> 49:34.387
and basically perfect in every way.

695
49:35.891 --> 49:39.305
I don't buy it. Tell me what it really means.

696
49:39.361 --> 49:42.561
- You don't trust me? - Nope.

697
49:43.253 --> 49:49.233
Tell me what it means, or I'm smearing paint all over you.

698
49:49.766 --> 49:52.394
- Hey! - Don't you dare.

699
49:52.419 --> 49:56.986
Tell me. Come on, tell me!

700
49:59.988 --> 50:03.999
- So that's how you wanna play? - What? What are you doing?

701
50:04.024 --> 50:06.357
- No! - You're getting it now.

702
50:06.382 --> 50:08.986
Vee! Vee!

703
50:09.658 --> 50:13.744
No! Just tell me, Vee!

704
50:14.845 --> 50:16.098
- Vee! - Stop!

705
50:41.799 --> 50:44.713
Oops... wrong cue.

706
50:47.638 --> 50:51.052
I'll just...

707
50:51.077 --> 50:55.681
leave this right here on the table.

708
50:56.016 --> 50:59.701
I'm leaving. Sugary sweet!

709
51:07.483 --> 51:09.680
So shall we finish this scene, Vee?

710
51:19.519 --> 51:21.661
We can end it here too. It's cute this way.

711
51:33.086 --> 51:37.185
Your cooking was amazing. I ate way too much.

712
51:38.320 --> 51:41.873
Chef Queen needs to come learn some recipes from you.

713
51:41.898 --> 51:43.146
Anytime.

714
51:47.554 --> 51:50.826
It's pouring. I don't think you should drive home.

715
51:53.364 --> 51:58.413
Exactly. Looks like I'll just have to stay the night.

716
52:14.792 --> 52:17.887
The rain's letting up. You could probably leave now.

717
52:21.083 --> 52:25.974
I'm so sleepy, Vee. My eyes are already closing.

718
52:31.315 --> 52:32.954
You're so sneaky.

719
52:35.319 --> 52:39.267
Your mom told me I used to sleep over here a lot as a kid.

720
52:40.255 --> 52:41.612
Yeah, you did.

721
52:41.637 --> 52:44.385
Did you ever sleep over at my house?

722
52:44.410 --> 52:46.980
Yeah. Quite a few times.

723
52:47.325 --> 52:50.232
Really? I don't remember that at all.

724
52:51.070 --> 52:54.426
Little Nana used to talk about getting married all the time.

725
52:54.659 --> 52:57.779
Married? What did I say?

726
53:02.484 --> 53:05.090
What are you drawing, Nana?

727
53:05.479 --> 53:08.949
- Me when I grow up. - And who's this?

728
53:11.004 --> 53:14.392
- That's my sweetheart. - You already have one?

729
53:14.868 --> 53:16.804
Not yet. I'll have one when I grow up,

730
53:16.829 --> 53:18.829
and we'll get married like this.

731
53:21.796 --> 53:25.958
That's you, Vee. You have to come to my wedding too.

732
53:31.282 --> 53:32.477
Really?

733
53:32.691 --> 53:34.580
Really. And there's more.

734
53:34.605 --> 53:36.909
What else? Tell me.

735
53:39.619 --> 53:44.033
You must be tired from golfing. Let's sit here and rest.

736
53:53.051 --> 53:54.929
Those flowers are so pretty.

737
53:54.954 --> 53:57.905
You like them? I can make you a flower crown.

738
53:57.930 --> 53:59.519
Then I'll make one too.

739
54:22.221 --> 54:23.793
This one's for you.

740
54:25.880 --> 54:27.627
Then this one's for you.

741
54:35.114 --> 54:37.429
- Thank you. - So pretty.

742
54:38.233 --> 54:39.622
Nana.

743
54:40.738 --> 54:41.904
What?

744
54:43.491 --> 54:46.300
When we grow up, let's get married.

745
54:46.616 --> 54:50.505
Okay. When I grow up, I'll marry you, Vee.

746
54:51.047 --> 54:53.563
- Promise? - Promise.

747
55:00.641 --> 55:04.637
Oh, I was precocious even back then.

748
55:05.322 --> 55:08.944
You've probably forgotten all about that promise by now.

749
55:11.020 --> 55:12.886
I did forget.

750
55:17.322 --> 55:19.737
But I won't forget it again.

751
55:29.051 --> 55:30.222
What do you mean?

752
55:32.547 --> 55:36.298
I'll admit, I barely remember any of what you just told me.

753
55:37.178 --> 55:39.178
But if I really said that back then,

754
55:39.713 --> 55:41.442
then I have to keep my promise.

755
55:49.539 --> 55:51.695
A promise you made when you were six?

756
55:54.615 --> 55:59.402
What if that six-year-old girl still stands by her promise...

757
56:04.821 --> 56:07.537
and she's here to claim it now?

758
56:13.281 --> 56:15.139
What would you say, Vee?

759
59:48.586 --> 59:51.831
Miss Nana, this is bad. Something serious has happened.

760
59:51.856 --> 59:54.759
The dead fish stink all the way into the houses.

761
59:54.784 --> 59:56.046
(No to polluted water!)

762
59:56.070 --> 59:58.347
But the fish floating dead are saltwater fish,

763
59:58.372 --> 59:59.744
not freshwater fish.

764
01:00:00.846 --> 01:00:04.564
Are you saying someone's trying to sabotage our course?

765
01:00:05.199 --> 01:00:07.516
So you think Pro Vee had something to do

766
01:00:07.541 --> 01:00:09.873
with the smear campaign against our course?

767
01:00:10.355 --> 01:00:12.410
She's done something like this before.

768
01:00:12.435 --> 01:00:13.993
Why wouldn't she do it again?

769
01:00:18.907 --> 01:00:23.141
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

770
01:00:24.009 --> 01:00:28.624
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

771
01:00:29.092 --> 01:00:33.564
♪ Together, we'll race toward the line ♪

772
01:00:34.276 --> 01:00:38.689
♪ Chasing the dream that's yours and mine ♪

773
01:00:39.351 --> 01:00:44.522
♪ In the end, I know we'll make it there ♪

774
01:00:44.547 --> 01:00:49.295
♪ Just one rule for you and me to share ♪

775
01:00:49.320 --> 01:00:52.681
♪ Promise you'll stay close to me ♪

776
01:00:52.706 --> 01:00:55.232
♪ Hold me in your arms so tenderly ♪

777
01:00:55.257 --> 01:01:00.735
♪ I've never bowed to anyone in sight ♪

778
01:01:00.760 --> 01:01:03.868
♪ But for you, I'd surrender without a fight ♪

779
01:01:03.893 --> 01:01:08.665
♪ Just take my hand and hold it tight ♪

780
01:01:09.955 --> 01:01:13.100
♪ And walk with me along the way ♪

781
01:01:13.125 --> 01:01:15.828
♪ No matter what it takes to win someday ♪

782
01:01:15.853 --> 01:01:21.451
♪ Sometimes this tender heart may despair ♪

783
01:01:21.476 --> 01:01:24.708
♪ But tell me, why should we care? ♪

784
01:01:24.733 --> 01:01:27.148
♪ When all we need is love that's fair ♪

785
01:01:27.173 --> 01:01:30.739
♪ In a love we share, no one has to win or lose ♪

786
01:01:32.774 --> 01:01:37.524
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

787
01:01:38.081 --> 01:01:42.673
♪ A thousand rounds, it'd still choose you ♪

788
01:01:43.151 --> 01:01:47.973
♪ One look in your eyes is all I need ♪

789
01:01:47.998 --> 01:01:51.500
♪ Oh, baby. I trust your sweet. ♪
